-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), Part V -- THE SEAT LAYER (layer 2).
--
-- SEAT: a worker, self-employed person, survivor, child or person with a disability who contributes to or may claim from the
-- Canada Pension Plan, asking whether and how much they must contribute, whether they qualify for a retirement pension or a
-- disability, survivor's or children's benefit, how much, and what they must do or tell the Minister.
-- (For Part V of the Regulations the questions are about applying, proving, being paid, appealing and the arithmetic of the
-- pension and its adjustments; whether and how much to contribute is for the Act's Part I and the Regulations' Parts I to IV.)
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the layer-1 modules imported above as the questions the person would ask.
-- Nothing here is new law. Every question takes plain inputs (yes/no, a number, a date, a choice from a list), one for each
-- fact the person can state, each with a @desc worded as the person would be asked; the layer-1 rule is then called. No rule is
-- restated here.
-- Where a layer-1 rule takes a MAYBE (a date that may not exist), the seat asks a yes/no question and a date, and builds the
-- JUST or NOTHING inside; the date is ignored when the answer is no.
-- Where a layer-1 rule is a power of the Minister (the person's liability) the question is "Can the Minister ...?" or
-- "May ...?"; where it is a duty on the person the question is "Must I ...?"; a judgment the text hands to the Minister
-- ("is satisfied", "deems necessary") is asked as a yes/no fact about what the Minister has found.
-- Rates in per cent, amounts in dollars, dates as year-month-day.

§ `Canada Pension Plan Regulations, Part V -- the questions of a person who contributes to or may claim from the Plan`

§§ `Interpretation (regulation 37)`

-- reg 37(1) "Canada child benefit": the deemed overpayment under section 122.61 of the Income Tax Act for a qualified dependant under seven.
@export Is this payment a Canada child benefit for Part V of the Canada Pension Plan Regulations (reg 37(1))?
GIVEN `it is the deemed overpayment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount the deemed overpayment determined under section 122.61 of the Income Tax Act (the Canada child benefit shown on your notice)?
      `it is for a child under seven` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in respect of a qualified dependant under seven years of age?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is this payment a Canada child benefit (reg 37(1))` `it is the deemed overpayment` `it is for a child under seven` MEANS
    `reg 37(1) — an amount is a Canada child benefit` `it is the deemed overpayment` `it is for a child under seven`

-- reg 37(1) "personal representative": the executor, administrator or heir (or other person with ownership or control) of the estate; if no estate, the survivor; if no survivor, the next of kin.
@export Am I the personal representative of a deceased person (reg 37(1))?
GIVEN `there is an estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an estate of the deceased person?
      `I am the executor, administrator or heir` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the executor, administrator or heir of the estate?
      `I own or control estate property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the ownership or control of property that is part of the estate?
      `there is a survivor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a survivor of the deceased person (the spouse or common-law partner, as the Act defines it)?
      `I am the survivor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you that survivor?
      `I am the next of kin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the next of kin of the deceased person?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I the personal representative of a deceased person (reg 37(1))` `there is an estate` `I am the executor, administrator or heir` `I own or control estate property` `there is a survivor` `I am the survivor` `I am the next of kin` MEANS
    `reg 37(1) — a person is the personal representative of a deceased person`
        `there is an estate` `I am the executor, administrator or heir` `I own or control estate property` `there is a survivor` `I am the survivor` `I am the next of kin`

-- reg 37(2) and (3): a person or agency authorized under regulation 57 to receive a deceased beneficiary's unpaid benefit may also apply and receive.
@export Am I entitled to make an application for the purposes of subsection 60(2) of the Act (reg 37(2))?
GIVEN `the Act already entitles me to apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does subsection 60(2) of the Act already entitle you to make the application?
      `I am authorized under regulation 57` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you (or the agency you act for) authorized under regulation 57 to receive a benefit payment unpaid at a beneficiary's death?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I entitled to make an application (reg 37(2))` `the Act already entitles me to apply` `I am authorized under regulation 57` MEANS
    `reg 37(2) — a person is entitled to make an application for the purposes of subsection 60(2) of the Act` `the Act already entitles me to apply` `I am authorized under regulation 57`

@export Am I entitled to receive benefits for the purposes of subsection 60(4) of the Act (reg 37(3))?
GIVEN `the Act already entitles me to receive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does subsection 60(4) of the Act already entitle you to receive the benefits?
      `I am authorized under regulation 57` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you (or the agency you act for) authorized under regulation 57 to receive a benefit payment unpaid at a beneficiary's death?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I entitled to receive benefits (reg 37(3))` `the Act already entitles me to receive` `I am authorized under regulation 57` MEANS
    `reg 37(3) — a person is entitled to receive benefits for the purposes of subsection 60(4) of the Act` `the Act already entitles me to receive` `I am authorized under regulation 57`

-- reg 37(4): the prescribed individual who is a "public officer".
@export Am I a prescribed individual for the definition "public officer" in subsection 104(1) of the Act (reg 37(4))?
GIVEN `I am employed in a federal institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in a federal institution?
      `my services are required by a federal institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your services required by a federal institution?
      `it is casual or temporary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that employment, or the requirement for your services, on a casual or temporary basis?
      `it is a student employment program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it under a student employment program?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I a prescribed individual for the definition public officer (reg 37(4))` `I am employed in a federal institution` `my services are required by a federal institution` `it is casual or temporary` `it is a student employment program` MEANS
    `reg 37(4) — an individual is a prescribed individual for the definition public officer in subsection 104(1) of the Act`
        `I am employed in a federal institution` `my services are required by a federal institution` `it is casual or temporary` `it is a student employment program`

§§ `My Record of Earnings (regulations 39 to 41)`

-- reg 39: the form of an application for a statement of the unadjusted pensionable earnings in my Record of Earnings.
@export Is my application for a statement of my earnings made as the Regulations require (reg 39)?
GIVEN way IS A `cr2 Way of applying for a statement of earnings` @desc How did you apply? One of: an application in writing to the Minister; an application to the Minister by way of the Internet on the electronic form prescribed for that purpose; an application made in some other way
      `I gave my name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your application include your name?
      `I gave my address with postal code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include your address, including the postal code?
      `I gave my Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include your Social Insurance Number?
      `I gave my postal code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include your postal code?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my application for a statement of my earnings made as the Regulations require (reg 39)` way `I gave my name` `I gave my address with postal code` `I gave my Social Insurance Number` `I gave my postal code` MEANS
    `reg 39 — an application for a statement of earnings is made as the Regulations require`
        way `I gave my name` `I gave my address with postal code` `I gave my Social Insurance Number` `I gave my postal code`

-- reg 40: the contributor's claim to written notice of a reduction in the Record of Earnings.
@export Must the Minister notify me in writing of a reduction in my Record of Earnings (reg 40)?
GIVEN `section 97(4) of the Act requires it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does subsection 97(4) of the Act require that you be notified of a reduction in the unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to your account?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Must the Minister notify me in writing of a reduction in my Record of Earnings (reg 40)` `section 97(4) of the Act requires it` MEANS
    `reg 40 — the contributor must be notified of the reduction in writing, addressed to the contributor's latest known address` `section 97(4) of the Act requires it`

@export Is the notice of a reduction in my Record of Earnings in the form the Regulations require (reg 40)?
GIVEN `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice in writing?
      `it is addressed to my latest known address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it addressed to you at your latest known address?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is the notice of a reduction in my Record of Earnings in the form required (reg 40)` `it is in writing` `it is addressed to my latest known address` MEANS
    `reg 40 — a notice of a reduction is in writing addressed to the contributor at the latest known address` `it is in writing` `it is addressed to my latest known address`

-- reg 41: the salary and wages on which a contribution has been made for me under a provincial pension plan (from the contributions and the plan's rate, a per cent figure).
@export What are the salary and wages on which a contribution has been made for me under a provincial pension plan (reg 41)?
GIVEN tier IS A Tier @desc Which contribution is it? One of: the base tier; the first additional tier; the second additional tier
      year IS A NUMBER @desc For which calendar year (for example 2024)?
      `my contributions` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the contributions of that kind required to be made by you in that year under the provincial pension plan in respect of salary and wages, in dollars?
      `the plan rate` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the provincial pension plan's contribution rate of that kind for that year, in per cent (for example 5.4 for 5.4 per cent)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What are the salary and wages on which a contribution has been made for me under a provincial pension plan (reg 41)` tier year `my contributions` `the plan rate` MEANS
    CONSIDER tier
    WHEN `the base tier` THEN `reg 41(1) — the salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made under a provincial pension plan` year `my contributions` `the plan rate`
    WHEN `the first additional tier` THEN `reg 41(2) — the salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made under a provincial pension plan` year `my contributions` `the plan rate`
    WHEN `the second additional tier` THEN `reg 41(3) — the salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made under a provincial pension plan` year `my contributions` `the plan rate`

§§ `Recovery of an overpayment (regulation 42)`

-- reg 42: the Minister may deduct an overpayment out of a benefit payable to me or my estate, if it does not cause undue hardship.
@export Can an overpayment I owe be deducted from a benefit payable to me or my estate (reg 42)?
GIVEN `I owe an overpayment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you or your estate or succession owe an overpayment (the indebtedness of subsection 66(2.1) of the Act)?
      `a benefit is payable to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a benefit payable to you or your estate or succession under the Act or under another Act or program the Minister administers?
      `the deduction` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is to be deducted, in dollars?
      `the benefit payable` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the benefit is payable, in dollars?
      `the overpayment owing` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the overpayment is still owing, in dollars?
      `it causes me hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the deduction cause you or your estate or succession undue hardship?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can an overpayment I owe be deducted from a benefit payable to me or my estate (reg 42)` `I owe an overpayment` `a benefit is payable to me` `the deduction` `the benefit payable` `the overpayment owing` `it causes me hardship` MEANS
    `reg 42 — an amount owing may be deducted and retained out of a benefit payable`
        `I owe an overpayment` `a benefit is payable to me` `the deduction` `the benefit payable` `the overpayment owing` `it causes me hardship`

§§ `Applying for a benefit, a division or an assignment (regulations 43 to 46.1)`

-- reg 43(1): an application for a benefit, a division or an assignment is submitted to the Minister in writing.
@export Is my application for a benefit, a division of pensionable earnings or an assignment of a retirement pension made as the Regulations require (reg 43(1))?
GIVEN `I submitted it in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you submit the application to the Minister in writing?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my application made as the Regulations require (reg 43(1))` `I submitted it in writing` MEANS
    `reg 43(1) — an application for a benefit, a division or an assignment is made as the Regulations require` `I submitted it in writing`

-- reg 43(1.1): a denied disability pension application is deemed, on request, to be a retirement pension application.
@export Is my denied application for a disability pension deemed to be an application for a retirement pension (reg 43(1.1))?
GIVEN `it was denied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your application for a disability pension denied?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth (for example 1962-03-01)?
      `the date I applied` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you apply for the disability pension?
      `the date it was denied` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the application denied?
      `I would have been entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you have been entitled to a retirement pension if you had applied for it when you applied for the disability pension?
      `the request is by me or for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the request that it be treated as a retirement pension application made by you or on your behalf?
      `the request is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the request in writing to the Minister?
      `the date of my request` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make the request?
      `the date I was notified of the denial` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you notified of the denial?
      `the denial was confirmed on appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the denial finally confirmed on appeal?
      `the date I was notified of the confirmation` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date were you notified of the confirmation? (any date if not applicable)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my denied application for a disability pension deemed to be an application for a retirement pension (reg 43(1.1))` `it was denied` `my date of birth` `the date I applied` `the date it was denied` `I would have been entitled` `the request is by me or for me` `the request is in writing` `the date of my request` `the date I was notified of the denial` `the denial was confirmed on appeal` `the date I was notified of the confirmation` MEANS
    `reg 43(1.1) — the application for a disability pension is deemed to be an application for a retirement pension`
        `it was denied` `my date of birth` `the date I applied` `the date it was denied` `I would have been entitled` `the request is by me or for me` `the request is in writing` `the date of my request` `the date I was notified of the denial`
        (IF `the denial was confirmed on appeal` THEN JUST `the date I was notified of the confirmation` ELSE NOTHING)

@export What is the last day for my request that a denied disability pension application be treated as a retirement pension application (reg 43(1.1)(b))?
GIVEN `the date I was notified of the denial` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you notified of the denial?
      `the denial was confirmed on appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the denial finally confirmed on appeal?
      `the date I was notified of the confirmation` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date were you notified of the confirmation? (any date if not applicable)
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day for my request (reg 43(1.1)(b))` `the date I was notified of the denial` `the denial was confirmed on appeal` `the date I was notified of the confirmation` MEANS
    `reg 43(1.1)(b) — the last day for the request` `the date I was notified of the denial` (IF `the denial was confirmed on appeal` THEN JUST `the date I was notified of the confirmation` ELSE NOTHING)

-- reg 43(2): the Minister must forward an application to the authority of a provincial plan in two cases.
@export Must the Minister forward my application to the authority of a provincial pension plan (reg 43(2))?
GIVEN `my whole benefit is payable under the provincial plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Because of a section 80 agreement with a province providing a comprehensive pension plan, is the whole of any benefit payable to you deemed to be payable under that plan?
      `my division can be determined under the provincial plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the division of unadjusted pensionable earnings be determined under that plan in accordance with the agreement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Must the Minister forward my application to the authority of a provincial pension plan (reg 43(2))` `my whole benefit is payable under the provincial plan` `my division can be determined under the provincial plan` MEANS
    `reg 43(2) — the Minister must forward the application to the authority charged under the provincial plan` `my whole benefit is payable under the provincial plan` `my division can be determined under the provincial plan`

-- reg 44(1): another person or agency may apply for a person who cannot manage their own affairs.
@export May an application for a benefit, a division or an assignment be made on behalf of a person who cannot manage their own affairs (reg 44(1))?
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied the person is incapable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied, by medical certificates or other documentary evidence, that the person is incapable of managing their own affairs because of infirmity, illness, insanity or other cause?
      `the other person is authorized by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the person or agency applying is authorized by or under a law of Canada or of a province to manage the person's affairs?
      `no one is so authorized` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Minister that no other person or agency is so authorized?
      `the Minister approves the other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister approved the person or agency applying?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May an application be made on behalf of a person who cannot manage their own affairs (reg 44(1))` `the Minister is satisfied the person is incapable` `the other person is authorized by law` `no one is so authorized` `the Minister approves the other person` MEANS
    `reg 44(1) — an application may be made on behalf of a person incapable of managing their own affairs`
        `the Minister is satisfied the person is incapable` `the other person is authorized by law` `no one is so authorized` `the Minister approves the other person`

-- reg 44(2): after a death, the personal representative or a child may apply for a division.
@export May I apply for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings after a death (reg 44(2))?
GIVEN `it is a division application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55, or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c), of the Act?
      `someone is deceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is either or both of the spouses, former spouses or former common-law partners deceased?
      `I am the personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the personal representative of the deceased?
      `I am a child of a deceased person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or is the person you act for, a child of any of those deceased persons?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May I apply for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings after a death (reg 44(2))` `it is a division application` `someone is deceased` `I am the personal representative` `I am a child of a deceased person` MEANS
    `reg 44(2) — an application for a division may be made after a death` `it is a division application` `someone is deceased` `I am the personal representative` `I am a child of a deceased person`

-- reg 45(1) and (2): withdrawing an application for a benefit.
@export May I withdraw my application for a benefit (reg 45(1))?
GIVEN `no payment has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has no payment of a benefit been made in respect of the application?
      `the date I applied` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make the application?
      `my notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your notice of withdrawal in writing?
      `my notice is sent before payment begins` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it sent to the Minister before payment of the benefit begins?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May I withdraw my application for a benefit (reg 45(1))` `no payment has been made` `the date I applied` `my notice is in writing` `my notice is sent before payment begins` MEANS
    `reg 45(1) — an applicant may withdraw an application for a benefit` `no payment has been made` `the date I applied` `my notice is in writing` `my notice is sent before payment begins`

@export Can my withdrawn application for a benefit still be used to decide whether I am eligible (reg 45(2))?
GIVEN `I withdrew it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you withdrawn the application under subsection 45(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can my withdrawn application for a benefit still be used to decide my eligibility (reg 45(2))` `I withdrew it` MEANS
    `reg 45(2) — the application may be used afterwards to determine the applicant's eligibility for a benefit` `I withdrew it`

-- reg 45(3) and (4): withdrawing an application for a division within 60 days of the decision.
@export What is the last day I may withdraw my application for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings (reg 45(3))?
GIVEN `the date I received notice of the decision` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you receive notification of the decision on the application?
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day I may withdraw my application for a division (reg 45(3))` `the date I received notice of the decision` MEANS
    `reg 45(3) — the last day to withdraw an application for a division` `the date I received notice of the decision`

@export May I withdraw my application for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings (reg 45(3))?
GIVEN `it is a division application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application for a division under section 55, or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c), of the Act?
      `the date I received notice of the decision` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you receive notification of the decision on the application?
      `the date I send my notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you send your notice of withdrawal to the Minister?
      `my notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your notice of withdrawal in writing?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May I withdraw my application for a division (reg 45(3))` `it is a division application` `the date I received notice of the decision` `the date I send my notice` `my notice is in writing` MEANS
    `reg 45(3) — an applicant may withdraw an application for a division` `it is a division application` `the date I received notice of the decision` `the date I send my notice` `my notice is in writing`

@export Can my withdrawn application for a division still be used to decide whether I am eligible for the division (reg 45(4))?
GIVEN `I withdrew it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you withdrawn the application for a division under subsection 45(3)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can my withdrawn application for a division still be used to decide my eligibility (reg 45(4))` `I withdrew it` MEANS
    `reg 45(4) — the application may be used afterwards to determine whether the person is eligible for the division` `I withdrew it`

@export Must I be given written notice that an approved division was withdrawn (reg 45(5))?
GIVEN `the division was approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the application for a division approved?
      `it was later withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it later withdrawn?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Must I be given written notice that an approved division was withdrawn (reg 45(5))` `the division was approved` `it was later withdrawn` MEANS
    `reg 45(5) — the Minister must give written notice of the withdrawal to the other spouse, former spouse or former common-law partner or their estates` `the division was approved` `it was later withdrawn`

-- reg 46 and 46.1: the form of a notification of a division, of a cancellation, of an assignment.
@export Is the notice I was given of the division of my pensionable earnings in the form the Regulations require (reg 46(2))?
GIVEN `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice in writing?
      `items that apply to me` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of the notice of a division` @desc Which of the items (a) to (g) of regulation 46(2) apply to your case? Item (g) applies only if the Minister deems the information necessary.
      `items in the notice` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of the notice of a division` @desc Which of those items does the notice contain?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is the notice of the division of my pensionable earnings in the form required (reg 46(2))` `it is in writing` `items that apply to me` `items in the notice` MEANS
    `reg 46(2) — a notification required by subsection 55(8) or 55.2(10) of the Act is effected as the Regulations require` `it is in writing` `items that apply to me` `items in the notice`

@export Which items does the notice of the division of my pensionable earnings still lack (reg 46(2))?
GIVEN `items that apply to me` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of the notice of a division` @desc Which of the items (a) to (g) of regulation 46(2) apply to your case? Item (g) applies only if the Minister deems the information necessary.
      `items in the notice` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of the notice of a division` @desc Which of those items does the notice contain?
GIVETH A LIST OF `cr2 Item of the notice of a division`
`Which items does the notice of the division still lack (reg 46(2))` `items that apply to me` `items in the notice` MEANS
    `reg 46(2) — the items a notification of a division still lacks` `items that apply to me` `items in the notice`

@export Is the notice that a division was made given in writing as the Regulations require (reg 46(1))?
GIVEN `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notification (under subsection 55.2(4) of the Act) given by notice in writing?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is the notice that a division was made given as the Regulations require (reg 46(1))` `it is in writing` MEANS
    `reg 46(1) — a notification required by subsection 55.2(4) of the Act is effected as the Regulations require` `it is in writing`

@export What is the last day on which my division may be cancelled (reg 46(3))?
GIVEN `the date the division was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the division made?
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day on which my division may be cancelled (reg 46(3))` `the date the division was made` MEANS
    `reg 46(3) — the last day to cancel a division under subsection 55.1(5) of the Act` `the date the division was made`

@export May my division be cancelled under subsection 55.1(5) of the Act (reg 46(3))?
GIVEN `the date the division was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the division made?
      `the date of the cancellation` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the cancellation made?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May my division be cancelled (reg 46(3))` `the date the division was made` `the date of the cancellation` MEANS
    `reg 46(3) — a division may be cancelled under subsection 55.1(5) of the Act` `the date the division was made` `the date of the cancellation`

@export Is the notice that an assignment was made given in writing as the Regulations require (reg 46.1(1))?
GIVEN `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notification (under subsection 65.1(5) of the Act) given by notice in writing?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is the notice that an assignment was made given as the Regulations require (reg 46.1(1))` `it is in writing` MEANS
    `reg 46.1(1) — a notification required by subsection 65.1(5) of the Act is effected as the Regulations require` `it is in writing`

@export Is the notice of the assignment of a portion of my retirement pension in the form the Regulations require (reg 46.1(2))?
GIVEN `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice in writing?
      `it states the commencing month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the month with which the assignment commences, in accordance with subsection 65.1(10) of the Act?
      `it states the portion assigned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the portion of the retirement pension assigned?
      `it states my right to reconsideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the right to make a request for a reconsideration referred to in subsection 81(1) of the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is the notice of the assignment in the form required (reg 46.1(2))` `it is in writing` `it states the commencing month` `it states the portion assigned` `it states my right to reconsideration` MEANS
    `reg 46.1(2) — a notification required by subsection 65.1(12) of the Act is effected as the Regulations require` `it is in writing` `it states the commencing month` `it states the portion assigned` `it states my right to reconsideration`

§§ `Cancelling a benefit (regulation 46.2)`

-- reg 46.2(1): a written request to cancel within 12 months of the day payment began.
@export What is the last day I may ask to cancel my benefit (reg 46.2(1))?
GIVEN `the day my benefit began to be paid` IS A DATE @desc On what date did payment of the benefit begin?
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day I may ask to cancel my benefit (reg 46.2(1))` `the day my benefit began to be paid` MEANS
    `reg 46.2(1) — the last day to ask for the cancellation of a benefit` `the day my benefit began to be paid`

@export May I still ask the Minister to cancel my benefit (reg 46.2(1))?
GIVEN `the day my benefit began to be paid` IS A DATE @desc On what date did payment of the benefit begin?
      `the date of my request` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you make the request?
      `my request is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your request in writing?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May I still ask the Minister to cancel my benefit (reg 46.2(1))` `the day my benefit began to be paid` `the date of my request` `my request is in writing` MEANS
    `reg 46.2(1) — a beneficiary's request that a benefit be cancelled is made in time and in writing` `the day my benefit began to be paid` `the date of my request` `my request is in writing`

-- reg 46.2(2): an application for a disability pension is deemed to be a request to cancel a retirement pension already in payment.
@export Is my application for a disability pension treated as a request to cancel my retirement pension (reg 46.2(2))?
GIVEN `I get a retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you applying for a disability pension while you get a retirement pension?
      `the date I am deemed disabled` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you deemed to have become disabled for the purpose of entitlement to the disability pension (any day of that month)?
      `the date my retirement pension became payable` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your retirement pension become payable (any day of that month)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my application for a disability pension treated as a request to cancel my retirement pension (reg 46.2(2))` `I get a retirement pension` `the date I am deemed disabled` `the date my retirement pension became payable` MEANS
    `reg 46.2(2) — the application for a disability pension is deemed to be a request for the cancellation of the retirement pension` `I get a retirement pension` `the date I am deemed disabled` `the date my retirement pension became payable`

-- reg 46.2(2.1): a comparable provincial benefit; 90 days after notice of the decision deeming the applicant disabled.
@export What is the last day I may ask to cancel my retirement pension after a provincial decision that I am disabled (reg 46.2(2.1))?
GIVEN `the date I received notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you receive notice of the decision deeming you to be disabled?
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day I may ask to cancel my retirement pension (reg 46.2(2.1))` `the date I received notice` MEANS
    `reg 46.2(2.1) — the last day to ask for the cancellation of the retirement pension` `the date I received notice`

@export May I ask to cancel my retirement pension because of a decision under a comparable provincial plan (reg 46.2(2.1))?
GIVEN `I get a retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you applying for a benefit under a provincial pension plan comparable to a disability pension while you get a retirement pension?
      `the date I am deemed disabled` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you deemed disabled for the purpose of entitlement to that benefit (any day of that month)?
      `the date my retirement pension became payable` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your retirement pension become payable (any day of that month)?
      `the day my retirement pension began to be paid` IS A DATE @desc On what day did payment of your retirement pension begin?
      `the date I received notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you receive notice of the decision deeming you to be disabled?
      `the date of my request` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you make the written request?
      `my request is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your request in writing to the Minister?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May I ask to cancel my retirement pension because of a comparable provincial decision (reg 46.2(2.1))` `I get a retirement pension` `the date I am deemed disabled` `the date my retirement pension became payable` `the day my retirement pension began to be paid` `the date I received notice` `the date of my request` `my request is in writing` MEANS
    `reg 46.2(2.1) — an applicant for a comparable provincial benefit may request the cancellation of the retirement pension`
        `I get a retirement pension` `the date I am deemed disabled` `the date my retirement pension became payable` `the day my retirement pension began to be paid` `the date I received notice` `the date of my request` `my request is in writing`

-- reg 46.2(2.2): cancelling the disability pension and having the retirement pension back, within 60 days.
@export What is the last day I may ask to cancel my disability pension and have my retirement pension reinstated (reg 46.2(2.2))?
GIVEN `the date I received notice of my entitlement` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you receive notice of your entitlement to the disability pension?
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day I may ask to cancel my disability pension (reg 46.2(2.2))` `the date I received notice of my entitlement` MEANS
    `reg 46.2(2.2) — the last day to ask for the cancellation of the disability pension` `the date I received notice of my entitlement`

@export May I ask to cancel my disability pension and have my retirement pension reinstated (reg 46.2(2.2))?
GIVEN `my disability application was deemed a request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you an applicant whose disability pension application was deemed a request to cancel your retirement pension (subsection 46.2(2))?
      `the date I received notice of my entitlement` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you receive notice of your entitlement to the disability pension?
      `the date of my request` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you make the written request?
      `my request is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your request in writing to the Minister?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May I ask to cancel my disability pension and have my retirement pension reinstated (reg 46.2(2.2))` `my disability application was deemed a request` `the date I received notice of my entitlement` `the date of my request` `my request is in writing` MEANS
    `reg 46.2(2.2) — an applicant may request the cancellation of the disability pension and the reinstatement of the retirement pension` `my disability application was deemed a request` `the date I received notice of my entitlement` `the date of my request` `my request is in writing`

-- reg 46.2(3): the Minister must grant a request made in any of the four ways.
@export Must the Minister grant my request to cancel (reg 46.2(3))?
GIVEN `I asked in writing within 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you ask in writing within 12 months of your benefit starting (subsection 46.2(1))?
      `I asked within 90 days of the provincial decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you ask in writing within 90 days of receiving notice of a decision under a comparable provincial plan (subsection 46.2(2.1))?
      `I asked within 60 days of my entitlement notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you ask in writing, as a person covered by subsection 46.2(2), within 60 days of receiving notice of your entitlement to the disability pension (subsection 46.2(2.2))?
      `my disability application was deemed a request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your request deemed to be made because you applied for a disability pension with a disability that began before your retirement pension did (subsection 46.2(2))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Must the Minister grant my request to cancel (reg 46.2(3))` `I asked in writing within 12 months` `I asked within 90 days of the provincial decision` `I asked within 60 days of my entitlement notice` `my disability application was deemed a request` MEANS
    `reg 46.2(3) — the Minister must grant the request` `I asked in writing within 12 months` `I asked within 90 days of the provincial decision` `I asked within 60 days of my entitlement notice` `my disability application was deemed a request`

-- reg 46.2(4): repaying the amount described in subsection 66.1(2) of the Act.
@export What is the last day I must repay the amount owing after my request to cancel is granted (reg 46.2(4))?
GIVEN `the date my request was granted` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your request granted?
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day I must repay after my request to cancel is granted (reg 46.2(4))` `the date my request was granted` MEANS
    `reg 46.2(4) — the last day to repay the amount described in subsection 66.1(2) of the Act` `the date my request was granted`

@export Am I repaying within the time the Regulations allow after my request to cancel is granted (reg 46.2(4))?
GIVEN `my request was granted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a request referred to in subsection 66.1(2) of the Act granted under this section?
      `the date my request was granted` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your request granted?
      `the date of my repayment` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you repay?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I repaying within the time allowed after my request to cancel is granted (reg 46.2(4))` `my request was granted` `the date my request was granted` `the date of my repayment` MEANS
    `reg 46.2(4) — a repayment is made within the time the regulation allows` `my request was granted` `the date my request was granted` `the date of my repayment`

§§ `Proving my age and identity (regulations 47 to 51)`

-- reg 47(1): the Minister determines age and identity on a birth certificate (or copy, or act of birth) or Commission information.
@export Must my age and identity be determined on the basis of a birth certificate or Commission information (reg 47(1))?
GIVEN `a birth certificate is available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a birth certificate, a copy of one or a copy of an act of birth available?
      `the Commission has given information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Canada Employment Insurance Commission made information about you available to the Minister under subsection 28.2(5) of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Must my age and identity be determined on a birth certificate or Commission information (reg 47(1))` `a birth certificate is available` `the Commission has given information` MEANS
    `reg 47(1) — the Minister must determine the person's age and identity on the basis of a document or information in subsection (1)` `a birth certificate is available` `the Commission has given information`

@export Can the Minister require my original birth certificate or a copy of my act of birth issued by the competent authority (reg 47(2))?
GIVEN `there are grounds to doubt my copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of your birth certificate or act of birth?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can the Minister require my original birth certificate (reg 47(2))` `there are grounds to doubt my copy` MEANS
    `reg 47(2) — the Minister may require the original birth certificate or a copy of the act of birth issued by the competent authority` `there are grounds to doubt my copy`

@export Can the Minister determine my age and identity from other information or evidence (reg 47(3))?
GIVEN `none of my documents are available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds to believe that none of the documents in paragraph 47(1)(a) (a birth certificate, a copy, or a copy of an act of birth) are available?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can the Minister determine my age and identity from other information (reg 47(3))` `none of my documents are available` MEANS
    `reg 47(3) — the Minister may determine the person's age and identity on the basis of any other information or evidence` `none of my documents are available`

@export Can the Minister determine my age and identity from my census records held by Statistics Canada (reg 47(4))?
GIVEN `the Minister cannot determine it otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister unable to determine your age and identity under any of subsections 47(1) to (3)?
      `Statistics Canada can supply it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it possible to determine them from information obtained from Statistics Canada under section 87 of the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can the Minister determine my age and identity from Statistics Canada information (reg 47(4))` `the Minister cannot determine it otherwise` `Statistics Canada can supply it` MEANS
    `reg 47(4) — the Minister may determine the person's age and identity on the basis of information obtained from Statistics Canada` `the Minister cannot determine it otherwise` `Statistics Canada can supply it`

@export Can the Minister accept the determination of my age made under the Old Age Security Act or a provincial pension plan (reg 49)?
GIVEN `my age was determined under the Old Age Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your age determined under the Old Age Security Act?
      `my age was determined under a provincial plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your age determined under a provincial pension plan?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can the Minister accept the determination of my age made elsewhere (reg 49)` `my age was determined under the Old Age Security Act` `my age was determined under a provincial plan` MEANS
    `reg 49 — the Minister may accept the determination of the person's age for the purposes of the Act` `my age was determined under the Old Age Security Act` `my age was determined under a provincial plan`

@export Can the Minister make a new determination of my age (reg 50)?
GIVEN `my age was determined under the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your age already been determined pursuant to the Regulations?
      `new facts have come to the Minister's attention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have facts not previously taken into account come to the Minister's attention?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can the Minister make a new determination of my age (reg 50)` `my age was determined under the Regulations` `new facts have come to the Minister's attention` MEANS
    `reg 50 — the Minister may make a new determination of the age of the person` `my age was determined under the Regulations` `new facts have come to the Minister's attention`

@export Does the request to Statistics Canada about me meet the prescribed conditions (reg 51(a))?
GIVEN `it is in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the request made in a form prescribed by the Chief Statistician?
      `it bears the signed consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it bear the signed consent of the person concerned, or of the person or agency that made the application for them (or, if there is none, of any other who would have been entitled to make it)?
      `it gives the information for a search` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it provide the information needed to make a proper search of the census records?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does the request to Statistics Canada about me meet the prescribed conditions (reg 51(a))` `it is in the prescribed form` `it bears the signed consent` `it gives the information for a search` MEANS
    `reg 51(a) — a request to Statistics Canada meets the prescribed conditions` `it is in the prescribed form` `it bears the signed consent` `it gives the information for a search`

@export May the information about me obtained from Statistics Canada be disclosed to this person (reg 51(b))?
GIVEN `they work for the Department` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an officer, clerk or employee of the Department of Employment and Social Development?
      `an agreement requires it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure required by an agreement entered into under section 105 of the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May the information about me from Statistics Canada be disclosed to this person (reg 51(b))` `they work for the Department` `an agreement requires it` MEANS
    `reg 51(b) — information obtained from Statistics Canada may be disclosed to a person` `they work for the Department` `an agreement requires it`

§§ `What I must set out or furnish to the Minister (regulations 52 to 54.1)`

