      `the Minister has asked in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister asked you in writing for the information or evidence?
      `items that apply to my case` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information or evidence under regulation 54(1)` @desc Which of the items of regulation 54(1) apply to your case?
      `items I have already given` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information or evidence under regulation 54(1)` @desc Which of those items have you already set out or furnished?
GIVETH A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information or evidence under regulation 54(1)`
`Which items must I still set out or furnish for my application for a division (reg 54(1))` `I am making the application` `the Minister has asked in writing` `items that apply to my case` `items I have already given` MEANS
    `reg 54(1) — the items the applicant still has to set out or furnish for a division` `I am making the application` `the Minister has asked in writing` `items that apply to my case` `items I have already given`

