§§ `Payment of my benefit (regulations 55 to 59)`

-- reg 55: a benefit may be paid to a person or agency on behalf of a beneficiary who cannot manage their own affairs.
@export Can the Minister direct that my benefit be paid to someone on my behalf because I cannot manage my own affairs (reg 55(1))?
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied I am incapable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied, on the information or evidence presented or required, that you are incapable of managing your own affairs because of infirmity, illness, insanity or other cause?
      `the payee is authorized by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the person or agency to be paid is authorized by or pursuant to a law of Canada or of a province to manage your affairs?
      `no one is so authorized` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Minister that there is no person or agency so authorized?
      `the Minister approves the payee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister approved the person or agency to be paid?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can the Minister direct that my benefit be paid to someone on my behalf (reg 55(1))` `the Minister is satisfied I am incapable` `the payee is authorized by law` `no one is so authorized` `the Minister approves the payee` MEANS
    `reg 55(1) — the Minister may direct that a benefit be paid on behalf of a beneficiary to a person or agency`
        `the Minister is satisfied I am incapable` `the payee is authorized by law` `no one is so authorized` `the Minister approves the payee`

@export May my benefit be paid to the person or agency the Minister has directed (reg 55(2))?
GIVEN `they undertook to administer the benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person or agency undertaken, in an agreement with the Minister, to administer and expend the benefit on your behalf in accordance with the terms of the agreement?
      `they undertook to furnish information and do what I must do` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it also undertaken to furnish any information or evidence, and to do anything that the Act or the Regulations require you to furnish or do?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May my benefit be paid to the person or agency the Minister has directed (reg 55(2))` `they undertook to administer the benefit` `they undertook to furnish information and do what I must do` MEANS
    `reg 55(2) — the benefit may be paid to the person or agency the Minister has directed` `they undertook to administer the benefit` `they undertook to furnish information and do what I must do`

@export Must the person or agency that is paid my benefit on my behalf account to the Minister (reg 55(3))?
