GIVETH A `cr2 Payee of a benefit payment unpaid at death`
`Who may be paid a benefit payment unpaid at the beneficiary's death (reg 57)` `an amount is payable to the deceased` `a payment came back after the death` `there is an estate` MEANS
    `reg 57 — the payee of a benefit payment unpaid at death` `an amount is payable to the deceased` `a payment came back after the death` `there is an estate`

-- reg 58(1): a single monthly payment of a benefit also payable under the Quebec Pension Plan.
@export Can the Minister direct that my benefit and my Quebec Pension Plan benefit be paid as a single monthly payment (reg 58(1))?
GIVEN `I was paid in December 1974` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Government of Canada pay you a benefit in December 1974 in respect of contributions made under the Act and under the Quebec Pension Plan?
      `I remain entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you remain entitled to the benefit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can the Minister direct that my benefit be paid as a single monthly payment (reg 58(1))` `I was paid in December 1974` `I remain entitled` MEANS
    `reg 58(1) — the Minister may direct that a single monthly payment be made` `I was paid in December 1974` `I remain entitled`

-- reg 59: withholding a benefit on 30 days' written notice until evidence is furnished and the Minister is satisfied.
@export What is the earliest day the Minister may start to withhold my benefit after giving me written notice (reg 59(1))?
GIVEN `the date of the written notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the written notice given to you?
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the earliest day the Minister may start to withhold my benefit (reg 59(1))` `the date of the written notice` MEANS
    `reg 59(1) — the earliest day payment of the benefit may be withheld` `the date of the written notice`

@export Can the Minister withhold my benefit from a given day (reg 59(1))?
GIVEN `evidence is required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is evidence required under the Act or the Regulations to determine your eligibility or continuing eligibility to receive the benefit?
      `the Minister has asked for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister requested that evidence?
      `I have not complied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you not complied with the request?
      `the Minister is not satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister not satisfied with the evidence you furnished?
      `the date of the written notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the written notice given to you?
      `the day withholding would start` IS A DATE @desc From what day would payment be withheld?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can the Minister withhold my benefit from a given day (reg 59(1))` `evidence is required` `the Minister has asked for it` `I have not complied` `the Minister is not satisfied` `the date of the written notice` `the day withholding would start` MEANS
    `reg 59(1) — the Minister may withhold payment of the benefit from a day`
        `evidence is required` `the Minister has asked for it` `I have not complied` `the Minister is not satisfied` `the date of the written notice` `the day withholding would start`

@export May the Minister keep withholding my benefit (reg 59(1))?
GIVEN `I have furnished the evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you furnished the evidence?
      `the Minister is satisfied of my eligibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied as to your eligibility to receive benefits?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May the Minister keep withholding my benefit (reg 59(1))` `I have furnished the evidence` `the Minister is satisfied of my eligibility` MEANS
    `reg 59(1) — payment of the benefit may still be withheld` `I have furnished the evidence` `the Minister is satisfied of my eligibility`

@export Am I paid for a day of the period my benefit was withheld, once payment resumes (reg 59(2))?
GIVEN `payment has resumed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has payment of the benefit that was withheld under subsection 59(1) been resumed?
      `I was entitled on that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to receive benefits on that day of the period of withholding?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I paid for a day of the period my benefit was withheld (reg 59(2))` `payment has resumed` `I was entitled on that day` MEANS
    `reg 59(2) — the benefit is paid for a day of the period of withholding` `payment has resumed` `I was entitled on that day`

§§ `Applying for a retirement pension, and the annual adjustment (regulations 61 and 62)`

-- reg 61: the statement of contributory salary and wages and contributory self-employed earnings an applicant for a retirement pension files.
@export For which years must I file a statement of my contributory earnings with my application for a retirement pension (reg 61)?
GIVEN `the year I apply` IS A NUMBER @desc In which calendar year are you making the application?
      `the Minister requires the year before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister require a statement for the year preceding the year of the application?
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`For which years must I file a statement of my contributory earnings (reg 61)` `the year I apply` `the Minister requires the year before` MEANS
    `reg 61 — the years for which the applicant must file a statement` `the year I apply` `the Minister requires the year before`

@export What is my basic monthly benefit after the annual adjustment, with the Regulations' rounding (reg 62)?
GIVEN `my amount before adjustment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount that would have been payable for the month if no adjustment had been made, in dollars (section 45(2)(a) of the Act)?
      `the Pension Index ratio` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the ratio that the Pension Index for the year bears to the Pension Index for the year before (section 45(2)(b) of the Act), for example 1.0235?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my basic monthly benefit after the annual adjustment (reg 62)` `my amount before adjustment` `the Pension Index ratio` MEANS
    `reg 62(1) — the basic monthly amount of a benefit after the annual adjustment` `my amount before adjustment` `the Pension Index ratio`

§§ `Proving a relationship or a death (regulation 63)`

@export Must the Minister use the information in paragraphs (a) to (c) to decide whether someone is my spouse, partner, child or parent, or has died (reg 63(1))?
GIVEN `it is a question of relationship or death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question whether a person is the spouse, common-law partner, child or parent of an applicant, contributor or other person subject to a division, or whether a person is deceased?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Must the Minister use the information in paragraphs (a) to (c) to decide a relationship or a death (reg 63(1))` `it is a question of relationship or death` MEANS
    `reg 63(1) — the Minister must use the information in paragraphs (a) to (c) to determine the question` `it is a question of relationship or death`

@export Must I furnish this certificate or copy to the Minister (reg 63(2))?
GIVEN `it is a certificate or a copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a certificate of marriage, birth, baptism or death, a copy of one, or a copy of an act of marriage, birth, baptism or death?
      `it may enable the determination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May it enable the Minister to make a determination of a relationship or of a death?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Must I furnish this certificate or copy to the Minister (reg 63(2))` `it is a certificate or a copy` `it may enable the determination` MEANS
    `reg 63(2) — the applicant or beneficiary must furnish the document to the Minister` `it is a certificate or a copy` `it may enable the determination`

@export Can the Minister require the original of the document I furnished (reg 63(3))?
GIVEN `there are grounds to doubt my copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of the document?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can the Minister require the original of the document I furnished (reg 63(3))` `there are grounds to doubt my copy` MEANS
    `reg 63(3) — the Minister may require the original of the document or the copy of the act issued by the competent authority` `there are grounds to doubt my copy`

@export Must I furnish other information or evidence about my relationship to the person (reg 63(4))?
GIVEN `no document is available or adequate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are none of the documents referred to in subsection 63(2) available or adequate?
      `the Minister has asked me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister requested other information or evidence respecting your relationship?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Must I furnish other information or evidence about my relationship to the person (reg 63(4))` `no document is available or adequate` `the Minister has asked me` MEANS
    `reg 63(4) — the applicant or beneficiary must furnish other information or evidence respecting their relationship` `no document is available or adequate` `the Minister has asked me`

§§ `The death benefit when the estate does not claim it (regulation 64)`

-- reg 64: only for the case where a death benefit is payable to someone other than the estate. A death on or after 1 January 2019 has no amount test.
@export Can a direction be given to pay the death benefit to someone other than the estate (reg 64(1))?
GIVEN `paragraph 71(2)(a) of the Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does paragraph 71(2)(a) of the Act apply?
      `the date of death` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the contributor die?
      `the estate has applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the estate applied for the death benefit?
      `the date the estate applied` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (any date if not applicable)
      `the death benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the death benefit, in dollars?
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the contributor died, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can a direction be given to pay the death benefit to someone other than the estate (reg 64(1))` `paragraph 71(2)(a) of the Act applies` `the date of death` `the estate has applied` `the date the estate applied` `the death benefit` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` MEANS
    `reg 64(1) — a direction under subsection 71(2) of the Act may be given for payment of the death benefit to a person other than the estate`
        `paragraph 71(2)(a) of the Act applies` `the date of death` (IF `the estate has applied` THEN JUST `the date the estate applied` ELSE NOTHING) `the death benefit` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings`

@export Who is paid the death benefit when the estate does not claim it (reg 64(1))?
GIVEN `someone paid or owes the funeral expenses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an individual or institution who has paid, or is responsible for the payment of, the deceased contributor's funeral expenses?
      `there is a survivor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a survivor of the deceased contributor?
      `there is next of kin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there next of kin of the deceased contributor?
GIVETH A `cr2 Payee of a death benefit other than the estate`
`Who is paid the death benefit when the estate does not claim it (reg 64(1))` `someone paid or owes the funeral expenses` `there is a survivor` `there is next of kin` MEANS
    `reg 64(1) — the payee of the death benefit when a direction is given` `someone paid or owes the funeral expenses` `there is a survivor` `there is next of kin`

@export How much of the death benefit may be paid to the person who paid the funeral expenses (reg 64(2))?
GIVEN `the actual funeral expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc What were the actual funeral expenses, in dollars?
      `the death benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the death benefit, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of the death benefit may be paid to the person who paid the funeral expenses (reg 64(2))` `the actual funeral expenses` `the death benefit` MEANS
    `reg 64(2) — the most that may be paid to the individual or institution that paid or is responsible for the funeral expenses` `the actual funeral expenses` `the death benefit`

@export How much of the death benefit remains to be directed after the funeral expenses are paid (reg 64(3))?
GIVEN `the actual funeral expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc What were the actual funeral expenses, in dollars?
      `the death benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the death benefit, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of the death benefit remains to be directed (reg 64(3))` `the actual funeral expenses` `the death benefit` MEANS
    `reg 64(3) — the remainder of the death benefit that may be directed as if there were no such individual or institution` `the actual funeral expenses` `the death benefit`

@export Who is paid the remainder of the death benefit (reg 64(3))?
GIVEN `there is a survivor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a survivor of the deceased contributor?
      `there is next of kin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there next of kin of the deceased contributor?
GIVETH A `cr2 Payee of a death benefit other than the estate`
`Who is paid the remainder of the death benefit (reg 64(3))` `there is a survivor` `there is next of kin` MEANS
    `reg 64(3) — the payee of the remainder` `there is a survivor` `there is next of kin`

§§ `Children and school (regulations 65 to 67)`

@export Do I maintain the deceased contributor's dependent children wholly or substantially (reg 65)?
GIVEN `what I provide` IS A NUMBER @desc How much maintenance do you, as survivor, provide for the dependent children, in dollars?
      `what everyone provides` IS A NUMBER @desc How much maintenance is provided for them by all persons other than the children and any other dependent child of the contributor (you included), in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Do I maintain the deceased contributor's dependent children wholly or substantially (reg 65)` `what I provide` `what everyone provides` MEANS
    `reg 65 — the survivor maintains the dependent children wholly or substantially` `what I provide` `what everyone provides`

@export Do I maintain the child of a deceased contributor (reg 65.1(a))?
GIVEN `I provided for the child until the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make financial provision for the child periodically until the contributor's death?
      `what I provided each period` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did you provide each period, in dollars?
      `the orphan's benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the orphan's benefit payable under the Act, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Do I maintain the child of a deceased contributor (reg 65.1(a))` `I provided for the child until the death` `what I provided each period` `the orphan's benefit` MEANS
    `reg 65.1(a) — a person maintains the child of a deceased contributor` `I provided for the child until the death` `what I provided each period` `the orphan's benefit`

@export Do I maintain the child of a disabled contributor (reg 65.1(b))?
GIVEN `I provide for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make financial provision for the child periodically?
      `what I provide each period` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you provide each period, in dollars?
      `the disabled contributor's child's benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the disabled contributor's child's benefit payable under the Act, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Do I maintain the child of a disabled contributor (reg 65.1(b))` `I provide for the child` `what I provide each period` `the disabled contributor's child's benefit` MEANS
    `reg 65.1(b) — a person maintains the child of a disabled contributor` `I provide for the child` `what I provide each period` `the disabled contributor's child's benefit`

@export Is the child in full-time or part-time attendance at a school or university (reg 66(1))?
GIVEN `the child attends an institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the child attend an educational institution that provides training or instruction of an educational, professional, vocational or technical nature?
      `the child is enrolled full-time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child enrolled in courses that constitute a course load the institution recognizes as full-time study?
      `the share of a full course load` IS A NUMBER @desc What share of a full course load do the child's courses make up (for example 0.5 for half)?
GIVETH A `cr2 Attendance at a school or university`
`Is the child in full-time or part-time attendance at a school or university (reg 66(1))` `the child attends an institution` `the child is enrolled full-time` `the share of a full course load` MEANS
    `reg 66(1) — the attendance of a child at a school or university` `the child attends an institution` `the child is enrolled full-time` `the share of a full course load`

@export Is the child considered to be in attendance during a school vacation (reg 66(2))?
GIVEN attendance IS A `cr2 Attendance at a school or university` @desc What attendance does the child have apart from the absence? One of: full-time attendance at a school or university; part-time attendance at a school or university; no attendance at a school or university
      reason IS A `cr2 Reason a child is absent from the educational institution` @desc Why is the child absent? One of: the child is not absent; the child is absent during a normal period of scholastic vacation; the child is absent because of illness; the child is absent for some other reason
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is the child considered to be in attendance during a school vacation (reg 66(2))` attendance reason MEANS
    `reg 66(2) — the child is considered to be in attendance during a normal period of scholastic vacation` attendance reason

@export Is the child who is absent because of illness considered to be in attendance (reg 66(3))?
GIVEN attendance IS A `cr2 Attendance at a school or university` @desc What attendance does the child have apart from the absence? One of: full-time attendance at a school or university; part-time attendance at a school or university; no attendance at a school or university
      reason IS A `cr2 Reason a child is absent from the educational institution` @desc Why is the child absent? One of: the child is not absent; the child is absent during a normal period of scholastic vacation; the child is absent because of illness; the child is absent for some other reason
      `the child resumed at once` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the child resume attendance at any educational institution immediately after the absence and during the same academic year?
      `the Minister found the child unable to resume` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister determined that the child is unable to resume attendance in the same academic year?
      `the child resumed the next academic year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the child resume attendance at any educational institution in the following academic year?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is the child absent because of illness considered to be in attendance (reg 66(3))` attendance reason `the child resumed at once` `the Minister found the child unable to resume` `the child resumed the next academic year` MEANS
    `reg 66(3) — the child absent because of illness is considered to be in attendance during the absence` attendance reason `the child resumed at once` `the Minister found the child unable to resume` `the child resumed the next academic year`

@export Is the child considered to be in attendance on this day, after the Minister found the child unable to resume (reg 66(4))?
GIVEN `the child is one found unable to resume` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child one referred to in paragraph 66(3)(b) (absent because of illness, found by the Minister unable to resume attendance in the same academic year)?
      `the end of the vacation` IS A DATE @desc What is the end of the normal period of scholastic vacation that follows the academic year in respect of which the child was determined unable to resume attendance?
      day IS A DATE @desc For which day?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is the child considered to be in attendance on this day (reg 66(4))` `the child is one found unable to resume` `the end of the vacation` day MEANS
    `reg 66(4) — the child is considered to be in attendance on a day` `the child is one found unable to resume` `the end of the vacation` day

@export Until when is a child who died or ceased to be a dependent child during an illness absence considered to have been in attendance (reg 66(5))?
GIVEN `the child was absent because of illness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the child absent from the educational institution because of illness?
      `the child died or ceased to be a dependent child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the child die, or cease to be a dependent child or disabled contributor's child, during the absence?
      `the date of the death or the change` IS A DATE @desc On what date did that happen?
GIVETH A DATE
`Until when is the child considered to have been in attendance (reg 66(5))` `the child was absent because of illness` `the child died or ceased to be a dependent child` `the date of the death or the change` MEANS
    `reg 66(5) — the last day the child is considered to have been in attendance` `the child was absent because of illness` `the child died or ceased to be a dependent child` `the date of the death or the change`

@export Must I file an attestation signed by my child that the child attended school (reg 67)?
GIVEN `I claim the child attended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you claim that a dependent child is or was, for a period, in full-time or part-time attendance at a school or university?
      `the child is 18 or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that dependent child 18 or more years of age?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Must I file an attestation signed by my child that the child attended school (reg 67)` `I claim the child attended` `the child is 18 or more` MEANS
    `reg 67 — the applicant or beneficiary must file an attestation signed by the child and supporting documentation` `I claim the child attended` `the child is 18 or more`

@export Does what I filed about my child's attendance meet the Regulations (reg 67)?
GIVEN `I filed the child's signed attestation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file with the Minister an attestation signed by the child?
      `I filed supporting documentation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file supporting documentation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does what I filed about my child's attendance meet the Regulations (reg 67)` `I filed the child's signed attestation` `I filed supporting documentation` MEANS
    `reg 67 — what is filed meets the regulation` `I filed the child's signed attestation` `I filed supporting documentation`

§§ `A disability pension: applying, proving, keeping, and getting it back (regulations 68 to 72)`

-- reg 68(1): what an applicant supplies about the person whose disability is claimed.
@export Which items must I still supply about the disability I claim (reg 68(1))?
GIVEN `I claim a disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you claim that you or some other person is disabled within the meaning of the Act?
      `items I have already supplied` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information on a claimed disability under regulation 68(1)` @desc Which of the items (a)(i) to (iv), (b) and (c) of regulation 68(1) have you already supplied?
GIVETH A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information on a claimed disability under regulation 68(1)`
`Which items must I still supply about the disability I claim (reg 68(1))` `I claim a disability` `items I have already supplied` MEANS
    `reg 68(1) — the items the applicant still has to supply` `I claim a disability` `items I have already supplied`

@export Can the Minister require me to supply a statement of my occupation and earnings for any period (reg 68(2)(a))?
GIVEN `my disability is to be or has been determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your disability to be, or has it been, determined pursuant to the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can the Minister require me to supply a statement of my occupation and earnings (reg 68(2)(a))` `my disability is to be or has been determined` MEANS
    `reg 68(2)(a) — the Minister may require the person to supply a statement of occupation and earnings for any period` `my disability is to be or has been determined`

@export Can the Minister require me to undergo special examinations and supply reports (reg 68(2)(b))?
GIVEN `my disability is to be or has been determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your disability to be, or has it been, determined pursuant to the Act?
      `the Minister deems it necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister deem the examination or report necessary for the purpose of determining your disability?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can the Minister require me to undergo special examinations and supply reports (reg 68(2)(b))` `my disability is to be or has been determined` `the Minister deems it necessary` MEANS
    `reg 68(2)(b) — the Minister may require the person to undergo special examinations and to supply reports` `my disability is to be or has been determined` `the Minister deems it necessary`

@export Will the reasonable cost of an examination or report the Minister required be reimbursed or advanced to me (reg 68(3))?
GIVEN `the Minister required it under 68(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the examination or report required under subsection 68(2)?
      `the cost is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the cost reasonable?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Will the reasonable cost of an examination or report the Minister required be reimbursed to me (reg 68(3))` `the Minister required it under 68(2)` `the cost is reasonable` MEANS
    `reg 68(3)(a) — the reasonable cost is paid by way of reimbursement or advance, as the Minister deems fit` `the Minister required it under 68(2)` `the cost is reasonable`

@export Is this travel or living expense part of the cost of my examination (reg 68(4))?
GIVEN `it is a travel or living expense` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the expense a travel or living expense of the person whose disability is to be determined, or of a person to accompany that person?
      `the Minister deems it necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister deem the expense necessary?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is this travel or living expense part of the cost of my examination (reg 68(4))` `it is a travel or living expense` `the Minister deems it necessary` MEANS
    `reg 68(4) — the expense is included in the cost` `it is a travel or living expense` `the Minister deems it necessary`

-- reg 68.1: "substantially gainful" is a salary or wages at least the maximum annual disability pension, (A x B) + C.
@export What is the maximum annual amount a person could receive as a disability pension (reg 68.1(1))?
GIVEN `the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average, in dollars?
      `the flat rate benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the flat rate benefit, calculated as provided in subsection 56(2) of the Act, for a month, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the maximum annual amount a person could receive as a disability pension (reg 68.1(1))` `the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average` `the flat rate benefit` MEANS
    `reg 68.1(1) — the maximum annual amount a person could receive as a disability pension` `the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average` `the flat rate benefit`

@export Is my work substantially gainful (reg 68.1(1))?
GIVEN `my yearly salary or wages` IS A NUMBER @desc What salary or wages does the occupation provide in a year, in dollars?
      `the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average, in dollars?
      `the flat rate benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the flat rate benefit, calculated as provided in subsection 56(2) of the Act, for a month, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my work substantially gainful (reg 68.1(1))` `my yearly salary or wages` `the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average` `the flat rate benefit` MEANS
    `reg 68.1(1) — an occupation is substantially gainful` `my yearly salary or wages` `the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average` `the flat rate benefit`

-- reg 69: once I am determined disabled the Minister may require examinations, reports and rehabilitation.
@export Can the Minister require me to undergo examinations and supply reports and statements while I receive a disability benefit (reg 69(1))?
GIVEN `I have been determined disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been determined to be disabled within the meaning of the Act?
      `the Minister requires it to decide on payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister require it for the purpose of determining whether any amount shall be paid, or continue to be paid, as a benefit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can the Minister require me to undergo examinations and supply reports and statements (reg 69(1))` `I have been determined disabled` `the Minister requires it to decide on payment` MEANS
    `reg 69(1) — the Minister may require the person to undergo special examinations, supply reports and supply statements of occupation and earnings` `I have been determined disabled` `the Minister requires it to decide on payment`

@export Can the Minister require me to undergo rehabilitation measures (reg 69(2))?
GIVEN `I have been determined disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been determined to be disabled within the meaning of the Act?
      `the Minister thinks I may benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister of the opinion that you may benefit vocationally from reasonable rehabilitation measures?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can the Minister require me to undergo rehabilitation measures (reg 69(2))` `I have been determined disabled` `the Minister thinks I may benefit` MEANS
    `reg 69(2) — the Minister may require the person to undergo reasonable rehabilitation measures` `I have been determined disabled` `the Minister thinks I may benefit`

@export Will the reasonable cost of an examination, report or rehabilitation measure the Minister required be reimbursed or advanced to me (reg 69(3))?
GIVEN `the Minister required it under section 69` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the examination, report or rehabilitation measure required under section 69?
      `the cost is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the cost reasonable?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Will the reasonable cost of a measure the Minister required be reimbursed to me (reg 69(3))` `the Minister required it under section 69` `the cost is reasonable` MEANS
    `reg 69(3)(a) — the reasonable cost is paid by way of reimbursement or advance, as the Minister deems fit` `the Minister required it under section 69` `the cost is reasonable`

@export Is this travel or living expense part of the cost of a measure the Minister required (reg 69(4))?
GIVEN `it is a travel or living expense` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the expense a travel or living expense of the disabled person or of a person to accompany that person?
      `the Minister deems it necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister deem the expense necessary?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is this travel or living expense part of the cost of a measure the Minister required (reg 69(4))` `it is a travel or living expense` `the Minister deems it necessary` MEANS
    `reg 69(4) — the expense is included in the cost` `it is a travel or living expense` `the Minister deems it necessary`

-- reg 70: failing without good cause to comply with a requirement of the Minister under section 69.
@export Can I be determined to have ceased to be disabled because I did not comply with the Minister's requirement (reg 70(1))?
GIVEN `I have been determined disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been determined to be disabled within the meaning of the Act?
      `I did not comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with a requirement of the Minister made under section 69?
      `compliance was a risk to my life or health` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would compliance have presented a significant risk to your life or health?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can I be determined to have ceased to be disabled because I did not comply (reg 70(1))` `I have been determined disabled` `I did not comply` `compliance was a risk to my life or health` MEANS
    `reg 70(1) — the person may be determined to have ceased to be disabled` `I have been determined disabled` `I did not comply` `compliance was a risk to my life or health`

@export Is my failure to comply with the Minister's requirement for good cause (reg 70(2))?
GIVEN `compliance was a risk to my life or health` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would compliance have presented a significant risk to your life or health?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my failure to comply for good cause (reg 70(2))` `compliance was a risk to my life or health` MEANS
    `reg 70(2) — the failure to comply is for good cause` `compliance was a risk to my life or health`

@export Is the time from which I am determined to have ceased to be disabled not earlier than the day I failed to comply (reg 70(1))?
GIVEN `the day I failed to comply` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you fail to comply?
      `the time the Minister specifies` IS A DATE @desc From what time does the Minister specify that you ceased to be disabled?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is the time I am determined to have ceased to be disabled not earlier than the day I failed to comply (reg 70(1))` `the day I failed to comply` `the time the Minister specifies` MEANS
    `reg 70(1) — the time the Minister specifies is not earlier than the day of failure to comply` `the day I failed to comply` `the time the Minister specifies`

@export Must I tell the Minister that I have returned to work (reg 70.1)?
GIVEN `I have been determined disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been determined to be disabled within the meaning of the Act?
      `I have returned to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you returned to work?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Must I tell the Minister that I have returned to work (reg 70.1)` `I have been determined disabled` `I have returned to work` MEANS
    `reg 70.1 — the person must inform the Minister without delay` `I have been determined disabled` `I have returned to work`

-- reg 71 and 72: a request for reinstatement of a disability pension, post-retirement disability benefit or disabled contributor's child benefit.
@export Is my request to have my disability pension reinstated made as the Regulations require (reg 71(1))?
GIVEN `I submitted it in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you submit the request to the Minister in writing?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my request for reinstatement made as the Regulations require (reg 71(1))` `I submitted it in writing` MEANS
    `reg 71(1) — a request for reinstatement is made as the Regulations require` `I submitted it in writing`

@export What is the last day I may ask to have my disability pension reinstated (reg 71(2))?
GIVEN `a day in the month I became incapable again` IS A DATE @desc On what date, or on which day of the month, did you become incapable again of working?
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day I may ask to have my disability pension reinstated (reg 71(2))` `a day in the month I became incapable again` MEANS
    `reg 71(2) — the last day to make the request` `a day in the month I became incapable again`

@export Is my request for reinstatement of my disability pension in time (reg 71(2))?
GIVEN `a day in the month I became incapable again` IS A DATE @desc On what date, or on which day of the month, did you become incapable again of working?
      `the date of my request` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you make the request?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my request for reinstatement of my disability pension in time (reg 71(2))` `a day in the month I became incapable again` `the date of my request` MEANS
    `reg 71(2) — the request is made in time` `a day in the month I became incapable again` `the date of my request`

@export Must the Minister decide whether my disability pension is reinstated on the information and evidence I furnished (reg 72(1))?
GIVEN `the question is whether I am entitled to reinstatement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question whether you are entitled to have a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit reinstated?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Must the Minister decide on the information and evidence I furnished (reg 72(1))` `the question is whether I am entitled to reinstatement` MEANS
    `reg 72(1) — the Minister must decide on the information and evidence furnished under subsection (2)` `the question is whether I am entitled to reinstatement`

@export Which items must I still furnish with my request for reinstatement (reg 72(2))?
GIVEN `my request includes my adult children's benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your request include a request to reinstate the disabled contributor's child benefit for your children who are 18 years of age or more?
      `items I have already furnished` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information on a request for reinstatement under regulation 72(2)` @desc Which of the items (a) to (g) of regulation 72(2) have you already furnished?
GIVETH A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information on a request for reinstatement under regulation 72(2)`
`Which items must I still furnish with my request for reinstatement (reg 72(2))` `my request includes my adult children's benefit` `items I have already furnished` MEANS
    `reg 72(2) — the items the applicant still has to furnish` `my request includes my adult children's benefit` `items I have already furnished`

§§ `Asking for a reconsideration or an appeal (regulations 74 to 74.2)`

@export May someone make a request for reconsideration or an appeal for me because I cannot manage my affairs (reg 74)?
GIVEN `the Minister or the Tribunal is satisfied I am incapable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister or the Social Security Tribunal satisfied, on medical certificates or other written statements, that you are incapable of managing your affairs?
      `the other person is authorized by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person or agency authorized by or under a law of Canada or of a province to manage your affairs?
      `no one is so authorized` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Minister or the Tribunal that there is no other person or agency so authorized?
      `the other person is considered qualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person or agency considered to be qualified to do so by the Minister or the Tribunal?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May someone make a request for reconsideration or an appeal for me (reg 74)` `the Minister or the Tribunal is satisfied I am incapable` `the other person is authorized by law` `no one is so authorized` `the other person is considered qualified` MEANS
    `reg 74 — a request for reconsideration or an appeal may be made on behalf of a person incapable of managing their affairs`
        `the Minister or the Tribunal is satisfied I am incapable` `the other person is authorized by law` `no one is so authorized` `the other person is considered qualified`

@export Which items must my request for reconsideration still set out (reg 74.1(1))?
GIVEN `the person asking is not the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person making the request someone other than the contributor?
      `items already set out` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of a request for reconsideration under regulation 74.1(1)` @desc Which of the items (a) to (c) of regulation 74.1(1) has the request already set out?
GIVETH A LIST OF `cr2 Item of a request for reconsideration under regulation 74.1(1)`
`Which items must my request for reconsideration still set out (reg 74.1(1))` `the person asking is not the contributor` `items already set out` MEANS
    `reg 74.1(1) — the items the request still has to set out` `the person asking is not the contributor` `items already set out`

@export Is my request for reconsideration made as the Regulations require (reg 74.1(1))?
GIVEN `I made it in writing to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the request in writing to the Minister?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my request for reconsideration made as the Regulations require (reg 74.1(1))` `I made it in writing to the Minister` MEANS
    `reg 74.1(1) — a request for reconsideration is made as the Regulations require` `I made it in writing to the Minister`

@export Can the Minister take steps to obtain information that my request left out (reg 74.1(2))?
GIVEN `my request fell short` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Minister that you failed to provide the information required by paragraphs 74.1(1)(a) to (c), or enough information to decide whether a longer period can be allowed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can the Minister take steps to obtain information that my request left out (reg 74.1(2))` `my request fell short` MEANS
    `reg 74.1(2) — the Minister may take any steps to obtain the information that is necessary to rectify the failure` `my request fell short`

@export What is the last day of the 365-day period after I was notified of the decision (reg 74.1(4)(a))?
GIVEN `the day I was notified` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you notified in writing of the decision or determination?
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day of the 365-day period after I was notified (reg 74.1(4)(a))` `the day I was notified` MEANS
    `reg 74.1(4)(a) — the last day of the 365-day period after the notification` `the day I was notified`

@export May the Minister allow me a longer period to ask for a reconsideration (reg 74.1(3) and (4))?
GIVEN `I have a reasonable explanation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that there is a reasonable explanation for requesting a longer period?
      `I showed a continuing intention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you demonstrated a continuing intention to request a reconsideration?
      `the day I was notified` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you notified in writing of the decision or determination?
      `the date of my request` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you make the request for reconsideration?
      `I applied again for the same benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied again for the same benefit?
      `I asked the Minister to rescind or amend` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you asked the Minister to rescind or amend the decision under subsection 81(3) of the Act?
      `my request has a reasonable chance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the request has a reasonable chance of success?
      `no one is prejudiced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that no prejudice would be caused to the Minister or a party by allowing a longer period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May the Minister allow me a longer period to ask for a reconsideration (reg 74.1(3) and (4))` `I have a reasonable explanation` `I showed a continuing intention` `the day I was notified` `the date of my request` `I applied again for the same benefit` `I asked the Minister to rescind or amend` `my request has a reasonable chance` `no one is prejudiced` MEANS
    `reg 74.1(3) — the Minister may allow a longer period to make a request for reconsideration`
        `I have a reasonable explanation` `I showed a continuing intention`
        (`reg 74.1(4) — the Minister must also be satisfied of a reasonable chance of success and no prejudice`
            `the day I was notified` `the date of my request` `I applied again for the same benefit` `I asked the Minister to rescind or amend`)
        `my request has a reasonable chance` `no one is prejudiced`

@export Is the notification of my appealable decision given as the Regulations require (reg 74.2)?
GIVEN `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notification in writing?
      `it was sent by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it sent by the Minister?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is the notification of my appealable decision given as the Regulations require (reg 74.2)` `it is in writing` `it was sent by the Minister` MEANS
    `reg 74.2 — a notification referred to in subsection 81(1) or (1.1) of the Act is given as the Regulations require` `it is in writing` `it was sent by the Minister`

§§ `The Pension Index (regulation 75)`

@export What is the Pension Index for the year, from the twelve monthly Consumer Price Index figures (reg 75)?
GIVEN `the twelve monthly figures` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What was the Consumer Price Index for each of the twelve months ending October 31 in the preceding year? (twelve figures)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the Pension Index for the year (reg 75)` `the twelve monthly figures` MEANS
    `reg 75(1) — the Pension Index for a year` `the twelve monthly figures`

§§ `Deductions from my benefit, and family allowance months (regulations 76 to 77)`

-- reg 76: recovering a provincial or municipal advance, assistance or welfare payment out of a lump sum, on the person's irrevocable written consent.
@export How much may be deducted from my lump sum and paid to the authority that paid me an advance or assistance (reg 76(2))?
GIVEN `the authority satisfied the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an authority (a provincial or municipal authority) satisfied the Minister that an excess payment was paid to you?
      `a lump sum is payable to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a one sum amount payable to you in accordance with subsection 62(1) of the Act for the period for which the excess payment was paid?
      `there is a written agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the Minister and the appropriate provincial official concluded an agreement in writing authorizing the deduction and payment?
      `the authority certified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the certification required by subsection 76(3) been received by the Minister?
      `my consent is irrevocable and in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your consent to the deduction and payment irrevocable and in writing?
      `the date I signed my consent` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you sign the consent?
      `the date the Minister received my consent` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the Minister receive it?
      `the excess payment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the excess payment, in dollars?
      `a deduction was already authorized` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a deduction and payment in respect of this excess payment already been authorized?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much may be deducted from my lump sum and paid to the authority (reg 76(2))` `the authority satisfied the Minister` `a lump sum is payable to me` `there is a written agreement` `the authority certified` `my consent is irrevocable and in writing` `the date I signed my consent` `the date the Minister received my consent` `the excess payment` `a deduction was already authorized` MEANS
    `reg 76(2) — the amount the Minister may authorize to be deducted and paid`
        `the authority satisfied the Minister` `a lump sum is payable to me` `there is a written agreement` `the authority certified` `my consent is irrevocable and in writing` `the date I signed my consent` `the date the Minister received my consent` `the excess payment` `a deduction was already authorized`

@export Can the Minister deduct an amount from my disability benefit and pay it to the administrator of a disability income program (reg 76.1(1))?
GIVEN `my benefit` IS A `Kind of benefit` @desc Which benefit is payable to you? One of: a retirement pension; a disability pension; a death benefit; a survivor's pension; a disabled contributor's child's benefit; an orphan's benefit; a post-retirement benefit; a post-retirement disability benefit
      `it is an amount described in subsection 65(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount one described in subsection 65(3) of the Act?
      `the administrator is approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the administrator approved by the Minister?
      `the administrator submitted my consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the administrator submitted to the Minister a record of the payment made under the disability income program, together with your irrevocable written consent?
      `the date I signed my consent` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you sign the consent?
      `the date the Minister received the documents` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the Minister receive those documents?
      `the amount` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can the Minister deduct an amount from my benefit and pay it to the administrator (reg 76.1(1))` `my benefit` `it is an amount described in subsection 65(3)` `the administrator is approved` `the administrator submitted my consent` `the date I signed my consent` `the date the Minister received the documents` `the amount` MEANS
    `reg 76.1(1) — the Minister may deduct an amount from a benefit and pay it to an administrator`
        `my benefit` `it is an amount described in subsection 65(3)` `the administrator is approved` `the administrator submitted my consent` `the date I signed my consent` `the date the Minister received the documents` `the amount`

-- reg 77: who counts as a "family allowance recipient", so that months of raising a child under seven may be left out of the contributory period.
@export Am I a family allowance recipient for the purposes of the Act (reg 77)?
GIVEN `the Act's definition already covers me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you described in the definition "family allowance recipient" in subsection 42(1) of the Act?
      `I am the spouse or partner of such a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the spouse, former spouse, common-law partner or former common-law partner of a person described in that definition as having received an allowance or a family allowance in respect of a child?
      `the child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is the child's date of birth?
      `the last day of the allowance period` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day of the period for which the allowance was received?
      `I stayed home to care for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you remain at home during that period as the child's primary caregiver?
      `those months are already or can be excluded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that period already been, or can it be, excluded or deducted from your contributory period under Part II of the Act?
      `I was an Armed Forces member posted abroad` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the Canadian Armed Forces who before 1973 was posted to serve outside Canada, or the spouse or former spouse of such a member?
      `I would have received the allowance but for the posting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc But for the posting, would you have received an allowance or family allowance for a child under seven years of age?
      `I am an eligible individual for the Canada child benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you considered, under section 122.62 of the Income Tax Act, to be an eligible individual for the Canada child benefit in respect of a qualified dependant under seven years of age?
      `I would have been eligible had a notice been filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you have been considered an eligible individual had a notice been filed under subsection 122.62(1) of the Income Tax Act?
      `nobody else was eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was no person considered to be an eligible individual in respect of the same qualified dependant?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I a family allowance recipient for the purposes of the Act (reg 77)` `the Act's definition already covers me` `I am the spouse or partner of such a person` `the child's date of birth` `the last day of the allowance period` `I stayed home to care for the child` `those months are already or can be excluded` `I was an Armed Forces member posted abroad` `I would have received the allowance but for the posting` `I am an eligible individual for the Canada child benefit` `I would have been eligible had a notice been filed` `nobody else was eligible` MEANS
    `reg 77(1) — a person is a family allowance recipient for the purposes of the Act`
        `the Act's definition already covers me` `I am the spouse or partner of such a person` `the child's date of birth` `the last day of the allowance period` `I stayed home to care for the child` `those months are already or can be excluded` `I was an Armed Forces member posted abroad` `I would have received the allowance but for the posting` `I am an eligible individual for the Canada child benefit` `I would have been eligible had a notice been filed` `nobody else was eligible`

§§ `Which months count as months of cohabitation (regulations 78 to 78.2)`

-- reg 78 (the division on divorce under section 55 of the Act) and reg 78.1 (the division of unadjusted pensionable earnings).
@export Does this separation interrupt our cohabitation (reg 78(2))?
GIVEN `the days we were separated` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days were you and your spouse separated?
      `it was for work or illness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend not to live separate and apart, and were you separated by reason of the occupation, employment or illness of either of you?
      `we had completed 36 months of cohabitation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had you completed the minimum period of 36 consecutive months of cohabitation required by paragraph 55(2)(a) of the Act before the separation?
      `we then lived together for over 90 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you subsequently resume cohabitation for a period of more than 90 days?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does this separation interrupt our cohabitation (reg 78(2))` `the days we were separated` `it was for work or illness` `we had completed 36 months of cohabitation` `we then lived together for over 90 days` MEANS
    `reg 78(2) — a separation interrupts the cohabitation of the former spouses` `the days we were separated` `it was for work or illness` `we had completed 36 months of cohabitation` `we then lived together for over 90 days`

@export From what day is our cohabitation deemed to have ceased because of an interruption (reg 78(3))?
GIVEN `the year the interruption began` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year did the interruption of more than 90 days begin (for example 2019)?
GIVETH A DATE
`From what day is our cohabitation deemed to have ceased (reg 78(3))` `the year the interruption began` MEANS
    `reg 78(3) — the first day of the year before which the cohabitation is deemed to have ceased` `the year the interruption began`

@export Is this a month during which we have cohabited, for the division under section 55 (reg 78(1))?
GIVEN `a day in the month` IS A DATE @desc Which month (give any date in it)?
      `we lived together in the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you live together as husband and wife in the month?
      `the month is during the marriage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the month during the marriage?
      `an interruption began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your cohabitation interrupted for more than 90 days (not saved by the rules in subsection 78(2))?
      `the year the interruption began` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, in which year did the interruption begin? (any number if not applicable)
      `the month is before our minimum 36 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the month precede the minimum period of 36 consecutive months of cohabitation required by paragraph 55(2)(a) of the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is this a month during which we have cohabited (reg 78(1))` `a day in the month` `we lived together in the month` `the month is during the marriage` `an interruption began` `the year the interruption began` `the month is before our minimum 36 months` MEANS
    `reg 78(1) — the month is a month during which the former spouses have cohabited`
        `a day in the month` `we lived together in the month` `the month is during the marriage`
        (IF `an interruption began` THEN JUST `the year the interruption began` ELSE NOTHING)
        `the month is before our minimum 36 months`

@export Is this a month during which we cohabited, for the division of pensionable earnings (reg 78.1(1))?
GIVEN `a day in the month` IS A DATE @desc Which month (give any date in it)?
      `we lived together in the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you live together in a conjugal relationship in the month?
      `the date we married or began to cohabit` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the marriage solemnized or did you commence to cohabit in a conjugal relationship, whichever applies?
      `dates of divorce annulment or separation` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On what dates were you divorced, was your marriage annulled, or did you commence to live separate and apart?
      `we had a long separation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you live separate and apart for one year or more and then resume cohabitation for at least one year?
      `the date we began to live apart` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date did you commence to live separate and apart? (any date if not applicable)
      `the date we resumed living together` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date did you resume cohabitation? (any date if not applicable)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is this a month during which we cohabited for the division of pensionable earnings (reg 78.1(1))` `a day in the month` `we lived together in the month` `the date we married or began to cohabit` `dates of divorce annulment or separation` `we had a long separation` `the date we began to live apart` `the date we resumed living together` MEANS
    `reg 78.1(1) — the month is a month during which the persons cohabited`
        `a day in the month` `we lived together in the month` `the date we married or began to cohabit` `dates of divorce annulment or separation`
        (IF `we had a long separation`
         THEN LIST (`cr2 Separation followed by resumed cohabitation` WITH
                        `the date they commenced to live separate and apart` IS `the date we began to live apart`
                        `they lived separate and apart for one year or more` IS TRUE
                        `the date they resumed cohabitation` IS `the date we resumed living together`
                        `they resumed cohabitation for at least one year` IS TRUE)
         ELSE EMPTY)

@export Have we cohabited for a continuous period of at least one year (reg 78.1(2))?
GIVEN `a day in the month we married or began to cohabit` IS A DATE @desc Give any date in the month in which the marriage was solemnized or you commenced to cohabit in a conjugal relationship.
      `a day in the month we began to live apart` IS A DATE @desc Give any date in the month in which you commenced to live separate and apart.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Have we cohabited for a continuous period of at least one year (reg 78.1(2))` `a day in the month we married or began to cohabit` `a day in the month we began to live apart` MEANS
    `reg 78.1(2) — the period of cohabitation is a continuous period of at least one year` `a day in the month we married or began to cohabit` `a day in the month we began to live apart`

@export Does our separation by reason of work or illness not interrupt our cohabitation (reg 78.1(3))?
GIVEN `we did not intend to live apart` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not have the intention to live separate and apart?
      `we were separated for work or illness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you separated by reason of the occupation, employment or illness of either of you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does our separation by reason of work or illness not interrupt our cohabitation (reg 78.1(3))` `we did not intend to live apart` `we were separated for work or illness` MEANS
    `reg 78.1(3) — the separation does not constitute interruption of cohabitation` `we did not intend to live apart` `we were separated for work or illness`

-- reg 78.2: the period of cohabitation for an assignment of a portion of a retirement pension.
@export Is this month in our period of cohabitation, for the assignment of a retirement pension (reg 78.2)?
GIVEN `we cohabited in the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the contributor and the spouse or common-law partner cohabit in the month?
      `it is the month we married or began to cohabit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the month in which the marriage was solemnized or you commenced to cohabit in a conjugal relationship?
      `it is in our joint contributory period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the month within your joint contributory period as defined in subsection 65.1(8) of the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is this month in our period of cohabitation (reg 78.2)` `we cohabited in the month` `it is the month we married or began to cohabit` `it is in our joint contributory period` MEANS
    `reg 78.2 — the month is in the period of cohabitation` `we cohabited in the month` `it is the month we married or began to cohabit` `it is in our joint contributory period`

§§ `Taking my retirement pension early or late (regulations 78.3 and 78.4)`

@export By what factor is my retirement pension reduced because it starts before the month I reach 65 (reg 78.3)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth (for example 1960-03-15)?
      `the month my pension starts` IS A DATE @desc In which month does your retirement pension become payable (give any date in it, for example 2024-01-01)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`By what factor is my retirement pension reduced because it starts before 65 (reg 78.3)` `my date of birth` `the month my pension starts` MEANS
    `reg 78.3 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable before the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` `my date of birth` `the month my pension starts`

@export By what factor is my retirement pension increased because it starts after the month I reach 65 (reg 78.4)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth (for example 1955-03-15)?
      `the month my pension starts` IS A DATE @desc In which month does your retirement pension become payable (give any date in it, for example 2023-01-01)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`By what factor is my retirement pension increased because it starts after 65 (reg 78.4)` `my date of birth` `the month my pension starts` MEANS
    `reg 78.4 — the adjustment factor for a retirement pension payable after the month the contributor reaches 65 years of age` `my date of birth` `the month my pension starts`
